{"step_index":95,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-28T17:10:02Z","thinking":"**Achieving Full Backend Success**\n\nI'm thrilled! All backend tests have passed with perfect precision. It's time to build a responsive, modern, mobile-first frontend application. This aligns with the reference image: SIH 2025 NATPAC Travel Data Collection + Tourism Explorer + AI Itinerary.\n\n\n**Defining Frontend Features**\n\nI've been meticulously defining the frontend features. I'm focusing on the header and navigation elements first, specifically branding and the crucial backend connection status indicator. The responsive tab bar will offer easy access to all the application's core functionalities. I am making sure the layout is intuitive for both desktop and mobile users, which aligns with the features in the specification. Next, I'll dive deep into each tab's unique requirements, starting with the NATPAC Travel Survey tab. I will be incorporating features like quick GPS auto-detect and smart AI trip parser inputs.\n\n\n**Designing Trip Log Functionality**\n\nI'm now deep in the design phase for the core trip logging feature. I'm focusing on rapid, one-click form filling, auto-suggestions for origins and destinations, and intuitive travel mode selection using icons. I am also working on adding fields for trip purpose, passenger count, fare, mood, and personal notes, all with a \"Log Trip & Submit\" button. I am thinking about adding a way to add a full timeline card for logged trips, with filters and badges. Lastly, I am going to have a direct database query access for developers.\n\n\n**Expanding Frontend Features**\n\nI am now fully updating the AI route planner tab, preserving the original route input. I am adding a new AI-powered multi-day tourism itinerary generator that considers specific destination types, durations, and budgets to provide a comprehensive daily breakdown. I also am making the real-world tourism explorer tab, incorporating live API integrations for global place searches with category filters and rich destination cards. Each card will provide details on food, sightseeing, accommodations, and activities.\n\n\n**Integrating Weather and Data**\n\nI'm now integrating live weather data via the Open-Meteo API, including temperature, conditions, humidity, and wind. I'm also adding a daily budget estimate and interactive maps, incorporating GIS coordinates. Finally, I'm integrating the best season for each destination.\n\n**Analyzing Trip Data**\n\nMy current focus is on a new tab for analytics. I'm designing high-level KPIs like total trips, survey distance, and estimated carbon savings, alongside interactive charts for mode split and peak travel hours. I am also planning an origin-destination commuter flows table, with a feature to export the full survey dataset to CSV.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Frontend generator script creating modern responsive PWA index.html, styles.css, main.ts, manifest, and service worker.\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"import os\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nWORKSPACE = Path(r\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\akhil\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\")\\nFRONTEND = WORKSPACE / \\\"frontend\\\"\\nSRC = FRONTEND / \\\"src\\\"\\n\\n# 1. frontend/manifest.webmanifest\\nmanifest_json = '''{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"TripTrail | NATPAC Mobile Travel Survey\\\",\\n  \\\"short_name\\\": \\\"TripTrail\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"NATPAC Mobile Travel Survey & Real-World Tourism Explorer (SIH 2025)\\\",\\n  \\\"start_url\\\": \\\"/\\\",\\n  \\\"display\\\": \\\"standalone\\\",\\n  \\\"background_color\\\": \\\"#0d131f\\\",\\n  \\\"theme_color\\\": \\\"#10b981\\\",\\n  \\\"orientation\\\": \\\"portrait-primary\\\",\\n  \\\"icons\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"https://cdn-icons-png.flaticon.com/512/854/854878.png\\\",\\n      \\\"sizes\\\": \\\"192x192\\\",\\n      \\\"