{"step_index":136,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-28T17:19:48Z","thinking":"**Defining Implementation Strategy**\n\nOkay, I'm focusing intently on the implementation plan, as directed. Right now, I'm going to create a detailed `walkthrough.md` document. It will include all changes made, the verification results, the commands run, the specific database technology and integrated APIs. This should fully address the user's focus on the implementation phase.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Comprehensive walkthrough artifact documenting the complete Python database migration, real-world tourism API integration, preserved & enhanced AI services, and full alignment with the NATPAC SIH 2025 mobile travel survey reference image.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# TripTrail & NATPAC Mobile Travel Survey Platform (SIH 2025) - Walkthrough\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\n\\nThe project has been migrated and enhanced into a **Python-based database & backend architecture (FastAPI + SQLite WAL / PostgreSQL)**. All original AI and routing capabilities have been preserved and extended, real-world public tourism APIs (**OpenStreetMap Nominatim**, **Wikivoyage MediaWiki**, and **Open-Meteo Weather**) have been integrated with local caching, and the application now fully fulfills the **Smart India Hackathon 2025 (Problem 25082 by NATPAC, Government of Kerala)** requirements shown in the reference image.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Database Architecture & Python Migration\\n\\n### Database Technology\\n- **Engine**: Python SQLite3 with Write-Ahead Logging (`PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;`) and Foreign Key enforcement.\\n- **PostgreSQL Support**: Can connect to external PostgreSQL if `DATABASE_URL` is set in `.env`, while defaulting to zero-configuration local SQLite (`data/triptrail.db`).\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: 100% compatible with existing REST contracts (`/api/status`, `/api/setup`, `/api/trips`, `/api/query`, `/api/ai/route`).\\n\\n### Relational Schema\\n```mermaid\\nerDiagram\\n    TRIPS {\\n        int id PK\\n        string title\\n        string location\\n        string start_date\\n        string end_date\\n        string origin\\n        string destination\\n        string departure_time\\n        string arrival_time\\n        string travel_mode\\n        string trip_purpose\\n        int passenger_count\\n        float fare_cost\\n        float distance_km\\n        int duration_min\\n        int is_auto_detected\\n        string mood\\n        string note\\n        timestamp created_at\\n    }\\n    DESTINATIONS {\\n        int id PK\\n        string name UK\\n        string state_region\\n        string category\\n        string description\\n        float latitude\\n        float longitude\\n        json food_cuisine\\n        json attractions\\n        json hotels\\n        json activities\\n        float ratings\\n        \n<truncated 6514 bytes>","Description":"\"Write walkthrough artifact summarizing all changes and verification results\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\akhil\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\b9e18599-ebc1-4ec3-9c72-c50606067964\\\\walkthrough.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing walkthrough.md\"","toolSummary":"\"Write walkthrough artifact\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
