{"step_index":138,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-28T17:19:59Z","content":"### Summary of Improvements & Deliverables\n\n#### 1. Database Technology & Python Architecture\n* **Backend**: Replaced the Node.js/pg backend with a high-performance **Python FastAPI backend** (`backend/app.py`).\n* **Database Engine**: Implemented **Python SQLite3 with Write-Ahead Logging (`WAL`)** mode (`data/triptrail.db`) with zero-configuration setup, while supporting external PostgreSQL instances via `DATABASE_URL` in `.env`.\n* **Schema**: Preserved all original `trips` table attributes and extended them with **NATPAC travel survey fields** (`trip_number`, `origin`, `destination`, `departure_time`, `arrival_time`, `travel_mode`, `trip_purpose`, `passenger_count`, `fare_cost`, `distance_km`, `duration_min`, `origin_lat`, `origin_lng`, `is_auto_detected`, `mood`, `note`).\n* **Raw SQL Compatibility**: Fully preserved the `/api/query` and `/api/status` endpoints for raw SQL query execution.\n\n#### 2. AI Functionality Preserved & Enhanced\n* **Preserved AI Route Planner (`/api/ai/route`)**: Retained OpenAI GPT-4o-mini and Google Routes API integrations. Added **Google Gemini API** (`google-genai` SDK) and a built-in rule-based NLP parser with Haversine distance estimation.\n* **AI Natural Language Trip Logger (`/api/ai/parse-trip`)**: Users can type or speak unstructured journey descriptions (e.g., *\"Took KSRTC bus from Trivandrum to Kollam at 8:30 AM for office work, paid 65 rs\"*), and the AI automatically extracts mode, origin, destination, time, purpose, and fare to populate the survey form.\n* **AI Smart Tourism Itinerary Planner (`/api/ai/itinerary`)**: Generates custom 2-to-7 day itineraries with daily schedules, local culinary recommendations, and sustainable transit modes.\n\n#### 3. Real-World Online Tourism APIs Integrated\n* **OpenStreetMap / Nominatim API**: Real-world geocoding and reverse geocoding to auto-fill location names, districts, roads, and coordinates.\n* **Wikivoyage / Wikipedia MediaWiki REST API**: Rich travel guide summaries, cultural heritage details, and sightseeing information.\n* **Open-Meteo\n<truncated 596 bytes>\neboat cruises, bamboo rafting, spice plantation walks, and Kathakali performances.\n  * 💰 **Approximate Costs & Budget**: Daily budget estimates per destination.\n  * 🌦️ **Live Weather & Seasonality**: Current climate data and ideal visiting seasons.\n\n#### 4. Features Implemented from Reference Image (SIH 2025 / NATPAC)\n* **Mobile Travel Survey Logger**: Trip sequence number, origin, destination, 📍 **GPS Auto-Detection**, departure/arrival times, travel mode selector (Bus, Train, Metro, Auto, Car, Bike, Walk, Bicycle, Ferry, Flight), trip purpose, passenger count, fare expenditure (₹), and mood.\n* **NATPAC Transportation Planning & GIS Analytics**:\n  * Key Performance Indicators (Total Trips, Distance, Duration, Passenger Volume, Estimated CO₂ Baseline).\n  * Modal Split breakdown chart (% share of public vs private transit).\n  * 24-Hour Peak Travel Hours departure histogram.\n  * Origin-Destination (OD) commuter corridor matrix.\n  * 📥 **Export to CSV**: Instant download of survey data for NATPAC researchers.\n* **Mobile & PWA Installation**: Mobile-responsive UI, bottom navigation bar, and installable PWA manifest with service worker.\n\n---\n\n### Setup and Run Instructions\n\n#### 1. Install Dependencies\n```bash\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n#### 2. Run the Application\n```bash\npython run.py\n```\nOpen your browser at **`http://localhost:8787`**.\n\n#### 3. Run Automated Tests\n```bash\npython -m unittest discover tests\n```\n\n#### Optional Configuration (`.env`)\n```env\nPORT=8787\nHOST=0.0.0.0\n\n# Optional: PostgreSQL Database (defaults to built-in SQLite data/triptrail.db)\n# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/triptrail\n\n# Optional: Live AI & Maps API Keys (app includes built-in NLP and OpenStreetMap fallbacks)\n# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\n# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIzaSy...\n# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=AIzaSy...\n```\n\nFor full architecture details and test results, please refer to [walkthrough.md](file:///C:/Users/akhil/.gemini/antigravity/brain/b9e18599-ebc1-4ec3-9c72-c50606067964/walkthrough.md).","truncated_fields":["content"]}
